01:10:30,040 --> 01:10:32,570
And he was really mad and
he was ripping my clothes.

1415
01:10:32,590 --> 01:10:34,910
- He did this to you?
- He was really scaring me.

1416
01:10:34,920 --> 01:10:36,670
I just didn't know where else to go.

1417
01:10:37,990 --> 01:10:39,240
Are you mad at me?

1418
01:11:40,340 --> 01:11:41,630
Rachel?

1419
01:11:41,700 --> 01:11:44,140
No, it's not Rachel. It's
Marty. Open the door.

1420
01:11:44,160 --> 01:11:45,620
Okay. Hang on.

1421
01:11:49,560 --> 01:11:50,750
What are you doing here?

1422
01:11:52,810 --> 01:11:54,230
Shame on you.

1423
01:12:03,950 --> 01:12:06,730
Hey, Dion. How you doing,
man? I really appreciate this.

1424
01:12:06,740 --> 01:12:08,240
This is my sister Rachel, by the way.

1425
01:12:08,260 --> 01:12:10,410
Rachel, this is my buddy,
my business partner, Dion.

1426
01:12:10,430 --> 01:12:11,660
- Hey.
- Hey.

1427
01:12:11,680 --> 01:12:13,000
Her place flooded.

1428
01:12:13,020 --> 01:12:15,200
She needs a place to crash
for the night. That's okay, right?

1429
01:12:15,210 --> 01:12:16,280
I don't know, man, it's...

1430
01:12:16,290 --> 01:12:19,300
I know, but I can't have her
exposed to mold and spores and shit.

1431
01:12:19,320 --> 01:12:22,500
D, come on, she's eight
months pregnant, all right?

1432
01:12:22,510 --> 01:12:23,750
Come on...

1433
01:12:23,760 --> 01:12:25,180
That's my nephew.

1434
01:12:25,200 --> 01:12:27,190
I'm not supposed to have people over.

1435
01:12:27,800 --> 01:12:31,180
She's got a bad situation at home. I
can't have her going back there. Please.

1436
01:12:31,200 --> 01:12:32,770
All right. Come on.
You can spend the night.

1437
01:12:32,790 --> 01:12:35,220
You just gotta be out of here by
tomorrow before my parents get back.

1438
01:12:35,230 --> 01:12:36,300
Okay. No problem.

1439
01:12:36,310 --> 01:12:38,060
We should take advantage
of the time we have together.

1440
01:12:38,070 --> 01:12:39,560
You know, really firm
up our business plan.

1441
01:12:39,570 --> 01:12:41,890
That way, when your dad gets
back, he sees how organized we are.

1442
01:12:41,900 --> 01:12:43,240
Yeah, he's pretty upset.

1443
01:12:43,260 --> 01:12:44,990
You left us with all of this
inventory for eight months.

1444
01:12:45,010 --> 01:12:47,020
That's fine. In a few weeks
I'll take the championship.

1445
01:12:47,030 --> 01:12:48,110
We'll be right back on track.

1446
01:12:48,120 --> 01:12:49,870
- Balls are right in here.
- Really? Where?

1447
01:12:49,890 --> 01:12:51,060
The top box.

1448
01:12:51,540 --> 01:12:52,540
Thanks.

1449
01:12:58,670 --> 01:13:01,040
- Whoa. You did the orange?
- Yep.

1450
01:13:01,050 --> 01:13:02,130
How'd you do the orange?

1451
01:13:02,150 --> 01:13:03,710
I contacted someone at Halex.

1452
01:13:03,720 --> 01:13:05,260
They colored the celluloid for me.

1453
01:13:05,280 --> 01:13:06,990
- How?
- Money, baby.

1454
01:13:07,760 --> 01:13:09,430
Me and my pop, we believe in you.

1455
01:13:09,450 --> 01:13:11,200
We're invested. That's
why he's been so mad.

1456
01:13:13,020 --> 01:13:14,680
Check it out, Rachel.

1457
01:13:14,700 --> 01:13:15,950
Here, check out the packaging.

1458
01:13:18,760 --> 01:13:21,470
"Marty Supreme. The official Marty
Mauser championship table tennis ball.

1459
01:13:21,480 --> 01:13:22,860
Professionally made. Orange..."

1460
01:13:22,880 --> 01:13:24,600
Orange spheres? You came up with that?

1461
01:13:24,610 --> 01:13:25,740
Yeah. Pretty good, right?

1462
01:13:25,760 --> 01:13:28,530
Pretty good? Dion,
this is... I'm stunned.

1463
01:13:29,130 --> 01:13:30,310
I'm stunned.

1464
01:13:30,330 --> 01:13:32,080
- Hand-drawn too.
- You drew this?

1465
01:13:32,100 --> 01:13:33,490
- Yeah.
- It's inspired.

1466
01:13:33,510 --> 01:13:34,370
I appreciate it.

1467
01:13:34,380 --> 01:13:36,340
I don't think you know
what you're capable of.

1468
01:13:36,350 --> 01:13:37,870
- Check it out.
- Thanks a lot.

1469
01:13:37,880 --> 01:13:39,130
Wow.

1470
01:13:39,150 --> 01:13:41,020
it's really nice.

1471
01:13:42,710 --> 01:13:44,780
- This is your room?
- No, it's my brother's.

1472
01:13:44,790 --> 01:13:46,220
You have a brother? You
never told me you had a brother.

1473
01:13:46,240 --> 01:13:47,650
It's a younger brother. He moved out.

1474
01:13:47,670 --> 01:13:48,960
So his room is free?

1475
01:13:49,260 --> 01:13:50,710
- Uh, yeah.
- Let me get my sister situated.

1476
01:13:50,720 --> 01:13:52,180
- I'll come find you in five minutes.
- Okay.

1477
01:13:52,200 --> 01:13:53,200
Five minutes.

1478
01:13:54,430 --> 01:13:55,990
I'm really impressed, D.

1479
01:13:56,010 --> 01:13:57,430
- Thank you.
- Seriously.

1480
01:13:58,380 --> 01:13:59,670
Special guy.

1481
01:13:59,690 --> 01:14:01,790
Let me get the bed
comfortable for you, all right?

1482
01:14:03,030 --> 01:14:04,310
So are you gonna go out there now?

1483
01:14:04,320 --> 01:14:06,390
Yeah, I gotta figure my
plan out for tomorrow.

1484
01:14:06,400 --> 01:14:07,640
Why? Plan for what?

1485
01:14:07,650 --> 01:14:10,200
Well, I need to get my head together.

1486
01:14:10,650 --> 01:14:12,150
How so?

1487
01:14:12,160 --> 01:14:15,410
This rich guy hit me up for a job. I
think I'm gonna get in touch with him.

1488
01:14:15,940 --> 01:14:18,110
- Really?
- Yeah.

1489
01:14:18,130 --> 01:14:20,660
- A job for what? What job?
- It doesn't matter. Just to get to Japan.

1490
01:14:21,280 --> 01:14:22,820
- For the championship?
- Yeah.

1491
01:14:23,330 --> 01:14:24,330
Wow.

1492
01:14:25,150 --> 01:14:28,120
Everything in my life is falling
apart, but I'm gonna figure it out.

1493
01:14:28,130 --> 01:14:29,970
Do you need any help? I could help you.

1494
01:14:29,980 --> 01:14:31,790
- No, it's all right. It's all right.
- Can I do anything?

1495
01:14:31,800 --> 01:14:33,130
Are you hungry?

1496
01:14:33,140 --> 01:14:34,850
- No.
- You sure?

1497
01:14:34,870 --> 01:14:37,210
Uh, I'll just be in the
other room, all right?

1498
01:14:40,140 --> 01:14:42,880
- Dion, I've never seen anything like this.
- I told you, man.

1499
01:14:42,900 --> 01:14:44,360
Man, we have to have a big catch-up

1500
01:14:44,380 --> 01:14:47,260
'cause this is the greatest thing that's
happened to me in the last eight months.

1501
01:14:47,270 --> 01:14:48,860
Who would've thought? Halex?

1502
01:15:01,500 --> 01:15:03,330
Good morning. Rockwell Ink.

1503
01:15:03,340 --> 01:15:05,800
Yes, hi, can I speak to
Milton Rockwell, please?

1504
01:15:05,820 --> 01:15:07,880
He's not in at the moment.
Can I take a message?

1505
01:15:07,900 --> 01:15:09,170
Okay, when are you expecting him?

1506
01:15:09,190 --> 01:15:11,120
Well, he's working off-site today.

1507
01:15:11,130 --> 01:15:12,970
- Again, can I take a message?
- It's hot.

1508
01:15:12,990 --> 01:15:14,300
Thank you so much.

1509
01:15:14,320 --> 01:15:16,210
Can you make some for my
sister for when she wakes up?

1510
01:15:16,220 --> 01:15:17,800
- She'll be really hungry.
- Hello?

1511
01:15:17,810 --> 01:15:19,250
You said off-site where?

1512
01:15:19,260 --> 01:15:21,060
I'm sorry, I can't give
you that information.

1513
01:15:21,080 --> 01:15:22,980
- Would you like to leave a message or not?
- Yes.

1514
01:15:23,000 --> 01:15:25,470
Can you apologize to him on my behalf?

1515
01:15:25,480 --> 01:15:27,470
I was the young gentleman that
was supposed to have breakfast

1516
01:15:27,480 --> 01:15:28,570
with him this morning.

1517
01:15:28,590 --> 01:15:30,990
- I'm not familiar.
- From his son's battalion.

1518
01:15:31,000 --> 01:15:33,810
I'm sorry, I-- I don't
know anything about that.

1519
01:15:33,820 --> 01:15:36,730
I have some personal belongings of
his son's I was supposed to give to him.

1520
01:15:36,740 --> 01:15:39,830
Letters and mementos and such,
but I messed up and I overslept.

1521
01:15:39,850 --> 01:15:42,790
I'm leaving town today, but I
could mail it to him if that's easier.

1522
01:15:42,810 --> 01:15:44,500
- No, no, no.
- No? Okay.

1523
01:15:44,880 --> 01:15:49,050
How about this, why don't you try
giving a call over to the Morosco Theatre.

1524
01:15:49,540 --> 01:15:50,910
The Morosco Theatre.

1525
01:15:50,920 --> 01:15:53,500
So, I'm like what? What am I doing?

1526
01:15:53,510 --> 01:15:55,340
Coming up here to wreck my night.

1527
01:15:55,360 --> 01:15:56,800
Honest, Mama, I didn't even
know you were coming here.

1528
01:15:56,820 --> 01:15:58,060
I'm through with you playing games.

1529
01:15:58,080 --> 01:15:59,310
I was just coming for a good time.

1530
01:15:59,330 --> 01:16:01,690
I heard this was where
all the call girls gather.

1531
01:16:03,810 --> 01:16:07,610
I'm trying to rebuild my life
here. Don't you understand that?

1532
01:16:07,630 --> 01:16:09,900
More like selling out
to the highest bidder.

1533
01:16:09,910 --> 01:16:12,400
You've got no right to judge me, Jed.

1534
01:16:12,420 --> 01:16:14,610
I fought tooth and nail for
every shred of happiness

1535
01:16:14,630 --> 01:16:16,900
- I've ever found while you...
- Right, and what did you give to me?

1536
01:16:16,920 --> 01:16:18,760
You never believed in me. Not once!

1537
01:16:20,250 --> 01:16:23,570
You wanna wallow in self-pity?
Well, here's an oven, Jed!

1538
01:16:23,580 --> 01:16:24,670
Alma!

1539
01:16:24,690 --> 01:16:25,750
I'm all right, Henry.

1540
01:16:25,770 --> 01:16:28,090
- Just give us a minute, please.
- My mama is a dirty bird.

1541
01:16:28,110 --> 01:16:30,090
Be careful now, Jedidiah.

1542
01:16:30,100 --> 01:16:34,720
And that fancy dress you put her in
is the only thing keeping in the stench!

1543
01:16:36,640 --> 01:16:38,890
Don't you lay a hand on my child.

1544
01:16:38,910 --> 01:16:40,620
I-I'm sorry, uh...

1545
01:16:45,550 --> 01:16:47,770
Mama, what did I do?

1546
01:16:47,790 --> 01:16:49,800
Go! Run!

1547
01:16:56,420 --> 01:16:58,820
- The door is locked.
- Oh, my God.

1548
01:16:58,840 --> 01:17:00,200
You've gotta be kidding me!

1549
01:17:00,220 --> 01:17:02,500
For Christ's sake, did
somebody put a latch on the door?

1550
01:17:02,520 --> 01:17:05,000
- Oh, God.
- I thought we had a good rhythm going.

1551
01:17:05,020 --> 01:17:08,280
A good rhythm going? On
what planet is that a good rhythm

1552
01:17:08,290 --> 01:17:09,710
- if you're alone in a room?
- I was in it.

1553
01:17:09,730 --> 01:17:12,480
It's like I wasn't even
there. In it? In what?

1554
01:17:12,490 --> 01:17:16,300
- Glenn, I couldn't get a word out.
- I understand. We're gonna fix it.

1555
01:17:16,320 --> 01:17:18,660
- That's what a rehearsal process is for.
- Fuck's sake.

1556
01:17:18,680 --> 01:17:20,880
Let's lose this, by the
way. Everybody take five.

1557
01:17:20,890 --> 01:17:22,310
Do me a favor, everybody...

1558
01:17:22,330 --> 01:17:24,600
Somebody needs to tell him something.

1559
01:17:24,620 --> 01:17:26,500
- It's impossible.
- Impossible.

1560
01:17:27,940 --> 01:17:29,730
- Do you want some water?
- Yes.

1561
01:17:29,750 --> 01:17:31,920
- Let me bring you some.
- God.

1562
01:17:35,810 --> 01:17:37,310
Hey, Kay.

1563
01:17:37,410 --> 01:17:39,080
Hey, it's Marty.

1564
01:17:41,750 --> 01:17:43,550
From London.

1565
01:17:44,500 --> 01:17:45,660
What are you doing here?

1566
01:17:45,680 --> 01:17:47,320
Well, I got a friend in
the stagehands union.

1567
01:17:47,340 --> 01:17:48,630
I was dropping something off for him.

1568
01:17:48,640 --> 01:17:50,750
- You watched that?
- Yeah, I hope that's okay.

1569
01:17:50,770 --> 01:17:51,880
Oh, God.

1570
01:17:51,900 --> 01:17:54,210
Hey, I can't believe
you're acting again.

1571
01:17:54,230 --> 01:17:56,380
That wasn't acting.
He won't let me act.

1572
01:17:56,400 --> 01:17:59,050
Yeah, no, that looked frustrating.
What's the deal with that guy?

1573
01:17:59,070 --> 01:18:00,340
Don't get me started.

1574
01:18:00,350 --> 01:18:02,060
Yeah, you were running
circles around him.

1575
01:18:02,890 --> 01:18:04,100
Of course I am.

1576
01:18:04,120 --> 01:18:05,730
Yeah. It was unbelievable.

1577
01:18:05,750 --> 01:18:07,390
He stays up for three days in a row

1578
01:18:07,410 --> 01:18:09,730
because his character
is supposed to be tired.

1579
01:18:09,750 --> 01:18:11,170
- It's obnoxious.
- Oh, God.

1580
01:18:13,010 --> 01:18:16,090
If he's so committed,
why'd he stop the scene?

1581
01:18:17,110 --> 01:18:18,990
Why didn't he punch his
hand through the screen,

1582
01:18:19,010 --> 01:18:20,430
unlock it from the other side?

1583
01:18:21,660 --> 01:18:23,450
- Right? That's what I would've done.
- Glenn!

1584
01:18:23,760 --> 01:18:25,260
- Yeah.
- Glenn!

1585
01:18:25,700 --> 01:18:27,700
- Yes. Thank you. Yes.
- I need to talk to you.

1586
01:18:30,260 --> 01:18:32,550
- Yes, what?
- What? What? What?

1587
01:18:32,570 --> 01:18:36,030
This kid understands the
character better than he does.

1588
01:18:36,040 --> 01:18:37,270
Excuse me?

1589
01:18:37,280 --> 01:18:38,630
- Tell him what you just told me.
- No, I don't want to.

1590
01:18:38,640 --> 01:18:39,430
No, tell him.

1591
01:18:39,450 --> 01:18:41,770
I was just saying you didn't really
seem like you were in the scene is all.

1592
01:18:42,630 --> 01:18:45,320
- Uh, who is this?
- He's nobody.

1593
01:18:45,340 --> 01:18:48,770
- That's the point.
- Also, you know, in my experience,

1594
01:18:50,020 --> 01:18:51,880
only children hold a knife like this.

1595
01:18:51,890 --> 01:18:53,560
If it's a serious fight, you
hold your knife like this,

1596
01:18:53,580 --> 01:18:54,950
- with the blade square to your wrist.
- This is not a street fight.

1597
01:18:54,970 --> 01:18:56,400
Okay, well, if you're
not going for realistic,

1598
01:18:56,410 --> 01:18:58,150
you might as well add a little flair.

1599
01:19:01,970 --> 01:19:03,130
Like that.

1600
01:19:03,140 --> 01:19:04,480
- Cut it out.
- Right, Kay?

1601
01:19:04,500 --> 01:19:06,750
Yeah, okay. Thanks for the
tutorial. Thank you very much.

1602
01:19:06,760 --> 01:19:10,860
Thank you very much indeed.
That's all we need today. Thank you.

1603
01:19:10,870 --> 01:19:12,630
- Best of luck, Kay. Best of luck.
- Get him out!

1604
01:19:12,650 --> 01:19:15,670
We no longer require your
presence. Thank you very much.

1605
01:19:15,690 --> 01:19:18,050
Well, with all due respect...

1606
01:19:18,070 --> 01:19:19,880
And yet every set
cost more than $5,000.

1607
01:19:19,900 --> 01:19:23,380
I can't just snap my fingers and get
your money and your wife into alignment.

1608
01:19:23,390 --> 01:19:24,890
I pay you to say no.

1609
01:19:24,900 --> 01:19:26,810
She seems to think
that this is carte blanche.

1610
01:19:26,830 --> 01:19:28,530
I can't just perform
the impossible here.

1611
01:19:28,550 --> 01:19:31,930
If you can't control her, I will
find someone else who can.

1612
01:19:32,240 --> 01:19:33,450
Asshole.

1613
01:19:38,490 --> 01:19:41,100
Mr. Rockwell. Mr. Rockwell.

1614
01:19:41,110 --> 01:19:43,710
- What?
- Hey. Marty Mauser. Nice to see you.

1615
01:19:43,740 --> 01:19:47,460
Did you call my office and
say you're friends with my son?

1616
01:19:47,620 --> 01:19:48,990
- Yes. But...
- Goddamn it!

1617
01:19:49,000 --> 01:19:51,070
I had no other way to get
in touch with you. Please.

1618
01:19:51,080 --> 01:19:52,710
I wanna revisit our
conversation about Japan.

1619
01:19:52,730 --> 01:19:54,950
I reconsidered it and I wanna
do it. I think it's a great idea.

1620
01:19:54,960 --> 01:19:56,870
The event's next week.
I've made alternate plans.

1621
01:19:56,880 --> 01:19:58,580
What other plans?
Okay, it was your idea.

1622
01:19:58,590 --> 01:20:01,620
It's a fantastic idea. Let's just have a
conversation about this for two seconds.

1623
01:20:01,630 --> 01:20:04,220
What are you doing?
Hey. Hey. Mr. Rockwell.

1624
01:20:04,240 --> 01:20:06,140
Please, let's both be
pragmatists about this.

1625
01:20:06,160 --> 01:20:08,310
Put your personal feelings
about me aside for a second.

1626
01:20:08,330 --> 01:20:11,390
You and I both know how much
value I would add with Endo.

1627
01:20:11,410 --> 01:20:13,270
In an exhibition on his home turf?

1628
01:20:13,290 --> 01:20:15,190
Imagine it. I'd be like
a stick of dynamite.

1629
01:20:15,210 --> 01:20:16,770
Whatever you have
planned, the alternative,

1630
01:20:16,790 --> 01:20:18,140
it's gonna pale in comparison.

1631
01:20:18,150 --> 01:20:19,360
Please give me two minutes.

1632
01:20:19,380 --> 01:20:22,520
We have enough common
ground to figure this out. Please!

1633
01:20:22,530 --> 01:20:25,070
- All right, get in the car.
- Really? Thank you.

1634
01:20:25,090 --> 01:20:26,300
Tommy, let's go.

1635
01:20:27,430 --> 01:20:29,990
Hey. Hey! Hey! Hey!

1636
01:20:30,440 --> 01:20:32,830
You son of a bitch.
I gave you the idea!

1637
01:20:43,220 --> 01:20:45,920
I'm sorry. Ms. Stone
wanted to let you know

1638
01:20:45,930 --> 01:20:47,760
that she'd love to have lunch with you.

1639
01:20:47,780 --> 01:20:49,370
- Ms. Stone?
- Yes.

1640
01:21:06,100 --> 01:21:07,610
My God, I'm so late.

1641
01:21:07,620 --> 01:21:09,200
Come on. What do you care?

1642
01:21:09,220 --> 01:21:11,740
You're the star. Gotta
feel pretty good, right?

1643
01:21:11,750 --> 01:21:13,610
I mean, why'd you even
stop in the first place?

1644
01:21:13,620 --> 01:21:16,210
I wanted security, and I got pregnant,

1645
01:21:17,130 --> 01:21:19,920
and he pressured me, and I settled.

1646
01:21:19,940 --> 01:21:22,340
Well, I mean, clearly, you're
doing the right thing now

1647
01:21:22,360 --> 01:21:24,510
and it sounds like he's
paying you back with interest.

1648
